/* v2.2 Q++ (character translation, not detail): Jill is the owner who cooks and serves, not staff. Her identity at
   phone scale is three masses — the long dark ponytail over her shoulder, a light warm figure (her own cream linen
   shirt with the sleeves rolled to the elbow, khaki trousers) among a room of darker, more saturated clothes, and a
   natural-linen half apron with the cat patch tied over it. No uniform white, no bib, no black trousers — the staff
   wear those. The fringe and the earrings are hers; style 4 (the tail) is never given to anyone procedural. */
const JILL_LOOK={skin:'#F5D2B8',hair:'#221712',hs:4,top:'#F3E9D6',pants:'#7A7052'};
/* ---- v2.4 rc6 (the player's 07:05, docs/v24/npc_wardrobe_0705_2026-10-02.txt): the generic guests' wardrobe. Not a
   shirt in a random saturated colour: each person is dressed — a quiet piece (a solid knit, a shirt), a refined one (a
   cardigan over a shirt, a jacket, a stripe, a check, a knit with a contrast trim) or, now and then, a statement (a
   floral, a small silk print, a tweed with its trim, a jewel-toned jacket) — every colour from one wardrobe of muted
   neutrals, blues, greens, warm reds and a few brights kept rare. A table has a rhythm (most quiet, some refined, a
   statement or two at most), never one palette; the Private Dining Room and the Lounge a little more dressed, the dining
   room the most casual. Named people, regulars, the staff and Jill keep their own clothes. The choices come from a
   hash of the day and a counter, never from Math.random, so a seeded day plays out exactly as before. ---- */
